        "procedure": "LaCl3·7H2O (372 mg, 1.0 mmol) and H4edta (292 mg, 1.0 mmol) were dissolved in water (10 mL). The mixture was adjusted to pH 7.0 by slow addition of 2.0 mol L−1 NaOH, then stirred for 0.5 h with addition of H3PO3 (246 mg, 3.0 mmol). The mixture was adjusted to pH 11.0 with 2.0 mol L−1 NaOH and heated at 80 °C for 18 h. After evaporation at room temperature for one month, colorless acicular crystals of 1 were isolated.",
